<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Wanjiku guesses the answers to three multiple-choice questions. Each question has four options, so each guess is right with probability <m>\dfrac{1}{4}</m>, independently.</p><p>A tree diagram with three stages may help. Write S when the event happens and F when it does not.</p><p>Give each probability exactly, as a fraction or an exact decimal.</p><p>(a) Find the probability that all three guesses are right.</p><div><fillin characters="8" name="ans1"/>  </div><p>(b) Find the probability that exactly two guesses are right.</p><div><fillin characters="8" name="ans2"/>  </div><p>(c) Find the probability that at least one guess is right.</p><div><fillin characters="8" name="ans3"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Each stage has two branches: S with probability <m>{\frac{1}{4}}</m> and F with probability <m>{\frac{3}{4}}</m>. The tree has eight paths; multiply along a path and add the paths you need.</p><p>(a) One path, SSS: <m>{\frac{1}{4}} \times {\frac{1}{4}} \times {\frac{1}{4}} = {\frac{1}{64}}</m>.</p><p>(b) Three paths have exactly two S: SSF, SFS and FSS. Each has probability <m>{\frac{1}{4}} \times {\frac{1}{4}} \times {\frac{3}{4}} = {\frac{3}{64}}</m>, so the answer is <m>3 \times {\frac{3}{64}} = {\frac{9}{64}}</m>.</p><p>(c) <q>At least one</q> is everything except FFF: <m>1 - ({\frac{3}{4}})^3 = 1 - {\frac{27}{64}} = {\frac{37}{64}}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{1}{64}</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{9}{64}</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{37}{64}</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>